  "provenance": {
    "pattern": "UK funky: a four-on-the-floor kick with soca and afro-house percussion rolling round it — hand drums and toms in a syncopated sixteenth pattern — a clap on two and four with extra ghost claps, and a sparse sub",
    "knowledge": "public knowledge of the genre: the pattern as drummers, producers and tutorials commonly write it; no recording was sampled, transcribed from audio or mined",
    "note": "Two bars: the kick keeps four; the hand drums play a tresillo-shaped line (the three-three-two) over the two bars with fills between; claps on two and four and a ghost on the a of three; closed hats on the offbeat, lightly swung. A sub held on the root with one move a bar."
  }
